Z||000003||Smoooooth GT||11-10-2001||10:53 PM||||HHmm...  as far as shaving the trim off... I used a flexable bondo type agent to fill in the channel where the trim was.. Fiberglassed over that and then skimmed again with glass and skimmed it with a very flexable bondo!!  I can grab the sail scoop and shake the car, pretty strong!! BUT, removing a panel now??  lol nooo way!! If I ever have to replace a panel, I'll have to redo the glass work again!! I'm not a bodywork wizard either.. I've been working on this car since October 2000!!! I'm in no hurry, but, I plan on being finished by Feb., I hope anyway's!! This car started out as a 1986 2m6!! It's taking me sooo long because of $$$ and I keep starting something else on the dang thing!!! I hope to finish sooon, as I want to show another forum member sooo bad, it's killing me!!  lol <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Smooooth_Yellow_sig_3.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig_blue_3.gif">  <BR>Shaved door hanles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, etc.... smooooth!!!||||reg||1
